Add the SMT1019 (r157 v2.0 wf1019) board device tree.

These four files come verbatim from the tablet-maker's SDK
(rk3576-linux6.1-20251118, kernel 6.1.118) and are not present in the
armbian/linux-rockchip tree: the board .dts, the two r157 board .dtsi
includes, and the MIPI panel definition (init sequence lives in the DT,
Rockchip-BSP style). All stock includes (rk3576s.dtsi, rk3576-rk806.dtsi,
rk3576-linux.dtsi) exist upstream. No dts Makefile entry is needed: the
dtb is built by kbuild's pattern rule via BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_INTREE_DTS_NAME,
same as the old SDK-tarball build.

